    <item>
      <title>Numeric in PostgreSQL</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/postgresql/numeric-in-postgresql/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 21 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/postgresql/numeric-in-postgresql/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;how-to-use-numeric-in-postgresql&#34;&gt;How To Use NUMERIC in PostgreSQL&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;PostgreSQL provides the NUMERIC data type for storing numeric values with high precision. This article will guide you through the usage of the NUMERIC type for accurate numeric calculations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;practical-example&#34;&gt;Practical Example&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sql&#34; data-lang=&#34;sql&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;-- Example: Using NUMERIC for precise calculations&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;CAST&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;123.456&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; NUMERIC) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this example, we cast a string to the NUMERIC type and perform a multiplication operation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;faqs-on-using-numeric-in-postgresql&#34;&gt;FAQs on Using NUMERIC in PostgreSQL&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div itemscope itemtype=&#34;https://schema.org/Question&#34; itemprop=&#34;mainEntity&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;h2 itemprop=&#34;name&#34;&gt;Q: What is the advantage of using NUMERIC over other numeric types?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div itemscope itemtype=&#34;https://schema.org/Answer&#34; itemprop=&#34;acceptedAnswer&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div itemprop=&#34;text&#34;&gt;The NUMERIC type in PostgreSQL offers higher precision compared to other numeric types. It is suitable for scenarios where precision is crucial, such as financial calculations, where rounding errors need to be minimized.&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div itemscope itemtype=&#34;https://schema.org/Question&#34; itemprop=&#34;mainEntity&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;h2 itemprop=&#34;name&#34;&gt;Q: Can I perform mathematical operations with NUMERIC and other numeric types?&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div itemscope itemtype=&#34;https://schema.org/Answer&#34; itemprop=&#34;acceptedAnswer&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div itemprop=&#34;text&#34;&gt;Yes, you can perform mathematical operations between NUMERIC and other numeric types. PostgreSQL will automatically convert between numeric types as needed for the operation.&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
